        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(net-policy): preserve diagnostics after redacted URL query secrets",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where redacting sensitive query values from URL-like diagnostic text could remove the trailing error detail after the secret value.\n\nThe fallback path in `redactSensitiveUrlLikeString()` handles arbitrary text that is not parseable as one complete URL. Its query-value regex previously consumed until `&`, so text such as:\n\n```text\nfailed https://x.test/cb?token=abc timed out\n```\n\ncould be reduced to:\n\n```text\nfailed https://x.test/cb?token=***\n```\n\nThat masked the secret, but it also dropped the useful diagnostic suffix: `timed out`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change keeps the redaction behavior narrow: sensitive query values are still replaced with `***`, but fallback matching stops before surrounding prose, whitespace, or common delimiters.\n\nAfter reviewer feedback, the fallback also handles balanced quoted values, unmatched quoted values, and wrapper-quoted diagnostics. This prevents `?token=\"abc\"`, `?token=\"abc timed out`, and git-style output such as `unable to access '...?token='abc timed out/'` from leaking the query secret or swallowing the diagnostic suffix.\n\nThe parseable full-URL path remains unchanged. This only tightens the heuristic fallback used for URL-like substrings inside larger diagnostic messages.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators and developers keep the remediation context in logs and CLI errors while secrets are still hidden.\n\nFor example, a message like:\n\n```text\nfailed https://x.test/cb?token=abc timed out\n```\n\nnow becomes:\n\n```text\nfailed https://x.test/cb?token=*** timed out\n```\n\ninstead of losing the timeout reason.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAdded focused regression tests in `packages/net-policy/src/redact-sensitive-url.test.ts` for arbitrary diagnostic text with sensitive query parameters followed by prose, balanced quoted values, unmatched quoted values, wrapper quotes, and bracket/delimiter-wrapped diagnostics.\n\nValidation run:\n\n```powershell\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run packages/net-policy/src/redact-sensitive-url.test.ts --reporter=verbose\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       21 passed (21)\ngit diff --check passed\n```\n\nReal CLI behavior proof through the shipped `openclaw plugins install` command, using a temporary valid config and failing git URLs so the real plugin install failure path formats git stderr through `redactSensitiveUrlLikeString()`:\n\n```powershell\n$env:OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH='.artifacts/net-policy-cli-proof-real/openclaw.json'\n$env:OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR='.artifacts/net-policy-cli-proof-real'\nnode scripts/run-node.mjs plugins install <git-spec> --force\n```\n\nCopied terminal output, with only the temporary clone directory normalized to `<TEMP>/repo`:\n\n```text\n[unquoted prose] exit=1\nfailed to clone github.invalid/openclaw/nope: Cloning into '<TEMP>/repo'...fatal: unable to access 'https://github.invalid/openclaw/nope.git?token=*** timed out/': URL rejected: Malformed input to a URL function\n\n[unmatched double quote] exit=1\nfailed to clone github.invalid/openclaw/nope: Cloning into '<TEMP>/repo'...fatal: unable to access 'https://github.invalid/openclaw/nope.git?token=\"*** timed out/': URL rejected: Malformed input to a URL function\n\n[unmatched single quote] exit=1\nfailed to clone github.invalid/openclaw/nope: Cloning into '<TEMP>/repo'...fatal: unable to access 'https://github.invalid/openclaw/nope.git?token='*** timed out/': URL rejected: Malformed input to a URL function\n\n[delimiter wrapped] exit=1\nfailed to clone github.invalid/openclaw/nope: Cloning into '<TEMP>/repo'...fatal: unable to access 'https://github.invalid/openclaw/nope.git?token=***), retrying/': URL rejected: Malformed input to a URL function\n```\n\nRelevant real command path:\n\n```text\nopenclaw plugins install <git-spec> --force\n  -> installPluginFromGitSpec(...)\n  -> git clone failure stderr\n  -> formatGitCommandFailure(...)\n  -> redactSensitiveUrlLikeString(...)\n  -> fallback URL-like query redaction\n  -> sensitive query value replacement while preserving diagnostic suffix text\n```\n\nNon-goals:\n\n- This does not replace the fallback with a full URL lexer.\n- This does not change userinfo redaction.\n- This does not broaden which query names are considered sensitive.\n\nAI-assisted: Yes, prepared with Codex GPT-5.5 xhigh review assistance.",
